# Blobbi standalone: build-time environment example.
# Copy what you need into an uncommitted `.env.local`, then restart Vite.

# Where "Enter Blobbi Island" sends the player. Defaults to the production
# Island (see src/config/ecosystem.ts). Point it at a local/staging Island here.
# VITE_BLOBBI_ISLAND_URL=http://localhost:8081

# Dev-only tools: the force-hatch / force-evolve buttons and the fixture
# worlds with their dev panel (`?fixture=egg|baby|adult|adult-v2`). Only
# honoured by `npm run dev`; production builds never read it.
# VITE_BLOBBI_DEV_TOOLS=true

# Dev server HTTPS (vite.config.ts only; the app never reads these). A phone
# on the LAN needs HTTPS for a REAL account (plain http://192.168.x.x has no
# crypto.randomUUID, which the relay connection needs); fixtures do not.
# Paths to a certificate and key the phone trusts (README: Testing on a phone).
# BLOBBI_DEV_TLS_CERT=./192.168.1.4+1.pem
# BLOBBI_DEV_TLS_KEY=./192.168.1.4+1-key.pem

# World travel on Nostr (M16): `nostr` makes the Blobbi's World Location (kind 31126, experimental) the authority for
# where it is, across devices and Blobbi worlds (src/features/presence/README.md). Unset: off, the Blobbi is simply home.
# The kinds are experimental (@blobbi-kit/core 0.11.0). Turning it on for a release is the owner's decision.
# VITE_BLOBBI_WORLD_TRAVEL=nostr
